00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:54.680
Episode 1 - Deep Breath
Airdate Aug 23

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:47.010
"Who frowned me this face?"
A slaughterhouse restaurant and a buried spaceship

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:54.850
lead The Doctor into a confrontation with
a long-forgotten foe...

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.040
Episode 2 - Into The Dalek
Airdate Aug 30

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.290
"Imagine the worst thing in the universe,
and then don't bother because you're looking

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:34.320
at right now. This is evil refined as engineering."

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:34.360
Episode 3 - Robot of Sherwood
Airdate Sept 6

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:34.690
"There's no such thing as Robin Hood!"
In a sun-dappled Sherwood Forest, The Doctor

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.610
discovers an evil plan from beyond the stars.
But with of Nottingham at stake (and possibly

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:37.590
Derby), there's no time for the two adventurers
to get into a fight about who is real and

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:38.050
who isn't - which is probably why they do
very little else!

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:38.300
Episode 4 - Listen
Airdate Sept 13

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.990
"What's that in the mirror, and the corner
of your eye? What's the footstep following,

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:41.820
but never passing by?"
What scares the grand old man of time? What

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.310
horrors lurk under his bed? Ghosts of the
past and future crowd into the lives of The

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:42.730
Doctor and Clara; a terrified caretaker in
a children's home, the last man standing in

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.110
the universe, and a little boy who doesn't
want to join the army...

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.370
Episode 5 - Time Heist
Airdate Sept 20

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.120
"Welcome to the bank of Karabraxos."
The Bank of Karabraxos is the deadliest bank

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.200
in the cosmos - only a fool or genius would
tempt to rob it. Fortunately, for The Doctor,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.850
he's both. But nothing even The Doctor has
encountered can prepare them for the Teller:

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.770
a creature of terrifying power that can detect
guilt.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.430
Episode 6 - The Caretaker
Airdate Sept 27

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:52.940
"Human beings have incredibly short life-spans.
Frankly, you should all be in a permanent

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:53.290
state of panic. Tick tock, tick tock."
Clara has it all under control: her life at

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:53.740
school, her life in space; her new boyfriend
and her mad old Time Lord. Everything is humming

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:53.800
along just fine, so long as everybody never
actually meets. And then, one morning, just

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:53.940
before assembly, Coal Hill welcomes a new
relief caretaker with a Scottish accent.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:54.010
Episode 7 - Kill The Moon
Airdate Oct 4

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:54.130
"The little planetoid that's been tagging
along beside you for a hundred years, which

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:54.280
gives you light at night and seas to sail,
is in the process of falling to bits."

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:54.610
In the near future, The Doctor and Clara arrive
on a decrepit shuttle making a suicide mission

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:57.120
to the Moon. Crashing on the lunar surface,
they find a mining base full of eviscerated

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.210
corpses, spider-like creatures scuttling about
in the dark, and a terrible dilemma.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.190
speeding among the stars of the future, a
legend is stalking the passengers. Once you

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.150
see the Mummy, you have 66 seconds to live.
Clara sees The Doctor at his most deadliest

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.080
and most ruthless - and finally she realises
she's made the right decision. Because this

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:01.120
is their last adventure: it's time to say
goodbye to the Time Lord.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.200
do you hide when event the walls are no protection.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:01.470
"D'you like the forest being in Trafalgar
Square? I think it's lovely."

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:01.510
One morning in London, and every city and
town in the world, the human race wakes up

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:01.550
to the most surprising invasion yet: the trees
have moved back in. Everywhere, in every land,

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:01.580
a forest has grown overnight and taken back
the Earth.

